  {
   "id": "mGcO0LbS0I4J",
   "from": "Michal Okoniewski",
   "author": "a188ee98eea3b027",
   "date": "2007-12-12T09:59:36Z",
   "subject": "Re: NaNs from RmaBackgroundCorrection? /exon array CDFs",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi Elizabeth &amp; Mark...\r<br>\r<br>I had also some difficulties with RMA,while started testing the CDFs\r<br>with the core one - as it is the smallest of the CDFs.\r<br>Probably some of the MM coordinate values are set strangely to some\r<br>small real value - keeping them 0 (or NA as in my CDFs)  should help -\r<br>hope so. :) See the session below.\r<br>\r<br>Cheers,\r<br>Michal\r<br>\r<br>==========\r<br>library(makecdfenv)\r<br>make.cdf.package(&quot;epcore.cdf&quot;, species=&quot;Homo_sapiens&quot;)  #renamed the\r<br>CDF to &quot;epcore.cdf&quot;\r<br>#after the package was created happily, intstalled it with R CMD\r<br>INSTALL...\r<br>\r<br>load(raw.data) #loading my favourite AffyBatch for exon chips\r<br>raw.data@cdfName &lt;- &quot;epcorecdf&quot;\r<br>library(simpleaffy)\r<br>x.rma.epc &lt;- call.exprs(raw.data) # the attempt to run RMA...\r<br>produces:\r<br>#Error in .local(object, ...) : subscript out of bounds\r<br>#In addition: Warning message:\r<br>#In .local(object, ...) : NAs introduced by coercion\r<br>\r<br>#so lets have a look inside the CDF:\r<br>library(epcorecdf)\r<br>ep.env &lt;- get(&quot;epcorecdf&quot;)\r<br>psets &lt;- ls(env=ep.env)\r<br>xxx &lt;- sapply(psets, function(x) get(x, env=ep.env))\r<br># Most of the probesets in xxx are OK, but:\r<br>xxx\r<br>\r<br>(...)\r<br>\r<br>$`2954500`\r<br>          pm            mm\r<br>[1,] 6378055 1.097175e-316\r<br>[2,] 2186565 1.097175e-316\r<br>[3,] 5591286 1.097175e-316\r<br>\r<br>(...)\r<br>\r<br>$`3414943`\r<br>          pm            mm\r<br>[1,] 4289597 6.017352e-317\r<br>[2,] 6176694 5.304990e-315\r<br>[3,] 2653954 4.113239e-317\r<br>[4,] 1289478 4.405324e-316\r<br>\r<br>$`3415027`\r<br>          pm            mm\r<br>[1,] 2941109 6.017352e-317\r<br>[2,] 2625289 5.304990e-315\r<br>[3,] 5775070 4.113239e-317\r<br>[4,] 2897369 4.393561e-316\r<br>\r<br>$`3415049`\r<br>          pm            mm\r<br>[1,] 5653924 4.393561e-316\r<br>[2,] 4707594 4.393276e-316\r<br>[3,] 4167571 9.881313e-324\r<br>[4,] 4469157 5.834065e-317\r<br>\r<br>$`3415095`\r<br>          pm\r<br>[1,] 5904707 4.387131e-316\r<br>[2,]   60576 9.881313e-324\r<br>[3,] 4597520 4.113239e-317\r<br>[4,] 1821844 4.387131e-316\r<br>\r<br>$`3415132`\r<br>          pm            mm\r<br>[1,] 2595100 4.384014e-316\r<br>[2,] 1607521 5.304990e-315\r<br>[3,] 4369309 4.113239e-317\r<br>[4,]  273268 4.384249e-316\r<br>\r<br>$`3415180`\r<br>          pm            mm\r<br>[1,]  769559  0.000000e+00\r<br>[2,] 6358321  0.000000e+00\r<br>[3,] 1312728 1.060998e-314\r<br>[4,] 1520209 7.634393e-317\r<br>\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
