  {
   "id": "8LcPHQL40_QJ",
   "from": "epurdom",
   "author": "43e2e19dd6bd2992",
   "date": "2007-12-12T17:36:44Z",
   "subject": "Re: NaNs from RmaBackgroundCorrection? /exon array CDFs",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi Michal,\r<br>Theoretically I always thought there shouldn&#39;t be &#39;mm&#39; probesets on\r<br>the array. But I know that this is not the case for the cdf, however,\r<br>since I have also gotten mm probes on something. This must be from\r<br>Affy&#39;s original (probeset level) cdf  but I have never checked this\r<br>out because we do the analysis on only the &#39;pm&#39; probes downstream. The\r<br>annotation on the RmaBackgroundCorrection function says that just the\r<br>&#39;pm&#39; is the default (option is &#39;typesToUpdate&#39;, I guess). So I doubt\r<br>this is the problem Mark was having, but he&#39;d have to respond to\r<br>that.\r<br>Best,\r<br>Elizabeth\r<br>\r<br>On Dec 12, 1:59 am, Michal Okoniewski &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">michal.okoniew...@gmail.com</a>&gt;\r<br>wrote:\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "&gt; Hi Elizabeth &amp; Mark...\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; I had also some difficulties with RMA,while started testing the CDFs\r<br>&gt; with the core one - as it is the smallest of the CDFs.\r<br>&gt; Probably some of the MM coordinate values are set strangely to some\r<br>&gt; small real value - keeping them 0 (or NA as in my CDFs)  should help -\r<br>&gt; hope so. :) See the session below.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Cheers,\r<br>&gt; Michal\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; ==========\r<br>&gt; library(makecdfenv)\r<br>&gt; make.cdf.package(&quot;epcore.cdf&quot;, species=&quot;Homo_sapiens&quot;)  #renamed the\r<br>&gt; CDF to &quot;epcore.cdf&quot;\r<br>&gt; #after the package was created happily, intstalled it with R CMD\r<br>&gt; INSTALL...\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; load(raw.data) #loading my favourite AffyBatch for exon chips\r<br>&gt; raw.data@cdfName &lt;- &quot;epcorecdf&quot;\r<br>&gt; library(simpleaffy)\r<br>&gt; x.rma.epc &lt;- call.exprs(raw.data) # the attempt to run RMA...\r<br>&gt; produces:\r<br>&gt; #Error in .local(object, ...) : subscript out of bounds\r<br>&gt; #In addition: Warning message:\r<br>&gt; #In .local(object, ...) : NAs introduced by coercion\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; #so lets have a look inside the CDF:\r<br>&gt; library(epcorecdf)\r<br>&gt; ep.env &lt;- get(&quot;epcorecdf&quot;)\r<br>&gt; psets &lt;- ls(env=ep.env)\r<br>&gt; xxx &lt;- sapply(psets, function(x) get(x, env=ep.env))\r<br>&gt; # Most of the probesets in xxx are OK, but:\r<br>&gt; xxx\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; (...)\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; $`2954500`\r<br>&gt;           pm            mm\r<br>&gt; [1,] 6378055 1.097175e-316\r<br>&gt; [2,] 2186565 1.097175e-316\r<br>&gt; [3,] 5591286 1.097175e-316\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; (...)\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; $`3414943`\r<br>&gt;           pm            mm\r<br>&gt; [1,] 4289597 6.017352e-317\r<br>&gt; [2,] 6176694 5.304990e-315\r<br>&gt; [3,] 2653954 4.113239e-317\r<br>&gt; [4,] 1289478 4.405324e-316\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; $`3415027`\r<br>&gt;           pm            mm\r<br>&gt; [1,] 2941109 6.017352e-317\r<br>&gt; [2,] 2625289 5.304990e-315\r<br>&gt; [3,] 5775070 4.113239e-317\r<br>&gt; [4,] 2897369 4.393561e-316\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; $`3415049`\r<br>&gt;           pm            mm\r<br>&gt; [1,] 5653924 4.393561e-316\r<br>&gt; [2,] 4707594 4.393276e-316\r<br>&gt; [3,] 4167571 9.881313e-324\r<br>&gt; [4,] 4469157 5.834065e-317\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; $`3415095`\r<br>&gt;           pm\r<br>&gt; [1,] 5904707 4.387131e-316\r<br>&gt; [2,]   60576 9.881313e-324\r<br>&gt; [3,] 4597520 4.113239e-317\r<br>&gt; [4,] 1821844 4.387131e-316\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; $`3415132`\r<br>&gt;           pm            mm\r<br>&gt; [1,] 2595100 4.384014e-316\r<br>&gt; [2,] 1607521 5.304990e-315\r<br>&gt; [3,] 4369309 4.113239e-317\r<br>&gt; [4,]  273268 4.384249e-316\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; $`3415180`\r<br>&gt;           pm            mm\r<br>&gt; [1,]  769559  0.000000e+00\r<br>&gt; [2,] 6358321  0.000000e+00\r<br>&gt; [3,] 1312728 1.060998e-314\r<br>&gt; [4,] 1520209 7.634393e-317"
